            <div xml:id="d339">

                <pb facs="0478" n="360" sameAs="frus:frus1928v02/pg360"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">125.643/55: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        the Minister in China</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >MacMurray</hi>)</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1928-10-04T15:00:00-05:00"><hi rendition="#italic">October 4,
                                1928—3 p.m.</hi></date></dateline></opener>
                <p>334. Your 719, September 20, 6 p.m. <hi rendition="#italic">New York Times</hi>
                    October 1 carries Associated Press story from Shanghai stating that plans for
                    reopening of Nanking Consulate are deadlocked because Nationalist officials
                    refuse to salute the American flag unless the United States should salute
                    first.</p>
                <pb facs="0479" n="361" xml:id="pg361"/>
                <p>What are the facts, where do the negotiations stand and what do you recommend?
                    Refer to Department’s telegram 300, August 31, 7 p.m., paragraph 5.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Kellogg</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
